WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.280
Test 4.

2
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.020
This is the IELTS listening test.

3
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:20.040
You will hear a number of different recordings and you will have to answer questions on what you hear.

4
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:28.040
There will be time for you to read the instructions and questions and you will have a chance to check your work.

5
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:32.040
All the recordings will be played once only.

6
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:35.160
The test is in four parts.

7
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:42.520
At the end of the test, you will be given ten minutes to transfer your answers to an answer sheet.

8
00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:59.720
You will hear a man asking a friend for advice on things to do in the city with a family of visitors.

9
00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:04.640
First, you have some time to look at questions 1 to 6.

10
00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:38.820
Now listen carefully and answer questions 1 to 6.

11
00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:47.660
<v MAN> Sandra, I seem to remember you had some family visitors staying with you recently.

12
00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.060
<v SANDRA> Yeah, that's right.

13
00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:52.420
<v SANDRA> My brother and his family were here a couple of months ago.

14
00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.620
<v MAN> OK, good.

15
00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:56.120
<v MAN> Well, I wanted to ask your advice.

16
00:01:56.540 --> 00:02:04.660
<v MAN> I've got my cousin and her family visiting next month and as I don't have kids, I've no idea where to take them.

17
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:05.540
<v SANDRA> Right.

18
00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:06.800
<v SANDRA> What about accommodation?

19
00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.300
<v SANDRA> Are they going to stay with you in your flat?

20
00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:10.580
<v MAN> No, thankfully.

21
00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:11.800
<v MAN> There wouldn't be room.

22
00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.700
<v MAN> My cousin wants me to recommend a hotel.

23
00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:16.200
<v MAN> Do you know anywhere?

24
00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:17.900
<v SANDRA> Yes, I do actually.

25
00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:21.620
<v SANDRA> I always recommend people stay at the King's Hotel.

26
00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:22.880
<v MAN> Where's that near?

27
00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:27.240
<v SANDRA> It's about five minutes walk from Murray Station, so nice and central.

28
00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.520
<v SANDRA> It's actually on George Street.

29
00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.200
<v MAN> Oh yes, I know.

30
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.980
<v MAN> I think they're on quite a tight budget.

31
00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.340
<v MAN> So how much, roughly, is it to stay there?

32
00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:42.320
<v SANDRA> If you book a family room, it's about £125 per night.

33
00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:49.220
<v SANDRA> My brother paid for two double rooms in the end and I think that was around £95 for each room.

34
00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.740
<v MAN> Oh, that's not too bad.

35
00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:53.400
<v SANDRA> So how old are your cousin's kids?

36
00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:54.580
<v MAN> Twelve and nine.

37
00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:58.020
<v MAN> So I want to organise some trips while they're here.

38
00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:04.620
<v MAN> I was thinking of doing a bus tour of the city centre as none of them have been here before.

39
00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.900
<v SANDRA> Those bus tours are quite expensive.

40
00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:10.180
<v SANDRA> I think it's better to do a walking tour.

41
00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.440
<v SANDRA> It gives you a much better feel for the city.

42
00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.280
<v SANDRA> There's one that starts from Colton Square.

43
00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:18.280
<v SANDRA> It takes a couple of hours and doesn't cost that much.

44
00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:19.600
<v MAN> Sounds good.

45
00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:20.660
<v MAN> I'll look that up.

46
00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:21.140
<v MAN> Thanks.

47
00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:25.080
<v SANDRA> If the weather's nice, one thing you could do is visit the old fort.

48
00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:27.040
<v SANDRA> You could get there by boat.

49
00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.800
<v SANDRA> The whole trip takes half a day.

50
00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:30.860
<v MAN> That's a really good idea.

51
00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:32.660
<v MAN> I'd like to do that myself.

52
00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:37.980
<v MAN> And if the weather's bad, I was thinking they could go to the Science Museum.

53
00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:41.440
<v MAN> But maybe they could do that when I'm at work.

54
00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:44.260
<v SANDRA> Yeah, don't forget it's closed on Mondays.

55
00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:49.940
<v MAN> They're here from Saturday for four nights, so Tuesday would be best, I think.

56
00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.000
<v SANDRA> And it won't be so crowded then.

57
00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:53.520
<v SANDRA> Saturdays are terrible.

58
00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:58.460
<v SANDRA> I took my kids to the exhibition on old computers there and it was far too crowded.

59
00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.160
<v SANDRA> I wanted to go back but it's finished now.

60
00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.180
<v MAN> That's a shame.

61
00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.940
<v MAN> My cousin's kids would have enjoyed that.

62
00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:09.200
<v SANDRA> There's another one starting soon on Space, which looks really good too.

63
00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.860
<v MAN> OK, well, I'll mention that to my cousin.

64
00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:21.140
Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions seven to ten.

65
00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:44.610
Now listen and answer questions seven to ten.

66
00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:50.570
<v SANDRA> Have you thought about where to take them to eat?

67
00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:55.130
<v MAN> Well, I really like all the food stalls at Clacton Market.

68
00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:57.430
<v MAN> My cousin's vegetarian.

69
00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:00.950
<v MAN> I know it's one of the best places for that kind of food.

70
00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:01.510
<v SANDRA> Definitely.

71
00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:04.410
<v SANDRA> And there'll be loads of choice for the kids too.

72
00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:06.730
<v SANDRA> You need to get there quite early though.

73
00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:10.770
<v SANDRA> At the weekend, most of the stalls stop serving lunch at 2.30. 

74
00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:14.270
<v MAN> Good point. It's all going to need careful planning.

75
00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:21.110
<v MAN> My cousin said she'd love to take the kids to a show at the theatre, but tickets are so expensive.

76
00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:21.970
<v SANDRA> I know.

77
00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:28.150
<v SANDRA> But you can get some good deals if you book online with bargain-tickets.com for the following day.

78
00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:31.690
<v SANDRA> On some seats there's a 75% discount.

79
00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:32.310
<v MAN> Really?

80
00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:34.490
<v MAN> I must try and get some.

81
00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:34.930
<v SANDRA> Yeah.

82
00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:37.830
<v SANDRA> There are lots of things you can do for free as well.

83
00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:39.410
<v SANDRA> No need to spend a fortune.

84
00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:40.410
<v MAN> Like what?

85
00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:42.450
<v SANDRA> They're coming next month, right?

86
00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:48.730
<v SANDRA> Well, check and see if it's the same weekend as the Roots Music Festival in Blakewell Gardens.

87
00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:51.770
<v MAN> R-O-O-T-S?

88
00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.670
<v SANDRA> Yeah, check it out online.

89
00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:57.450
<v SANDRA> It's always a family-friendly event and there's no entry charge.

90
00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:58.670
<v MAN> That sounds perfect.

91
00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:02.650
<v SANDRA> And if you're in Blakewell Gardens, climb Telegraph Hill.

92
00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:05.330
<v SANDRA> You'll be able to look right down on the port.

93
00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:08.570
<v SANDRA> Everyone's always really impressed because it's so huge.

94
00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:11.690
<v MAN> Oh yeah, I've been meaning to do that for ages.

95
00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:13.990
<v MAN> I've heard the view's amazing.

96
00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:15.870
<v SANDRA> Yeah, it's really worth the effort.

97
00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:19.350
<v MAN> Well, that's given me loads of ideas.

98
00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:20.570
<v MAN> Thanks so much.

99
00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:26.010
That is the end of part one.

100
00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:30.790
You now have one minute to check your answers to part one.
